{
  "_comment": [
    "Coarse semantic classes for nouns, used by QA and never shown to a learner.",
    "",
    "Why this exists rather than the browse category. The categories on the Words",
    "screen are topical: 의사 (doctor) is filed under body-health beside 배 and 약,",
    "because that is where a learner would look for it. The Level Test builder was",
    "refusing a distractor from the same *category*, which meant 거지 could be",
    "offered against 의사 — 길에 거지가 있었어요 and 길에 의사가 있었어요 are both",
    "ordinary Korean, and the item has two answers.",
    "",
    "It is also what the composed-sentence safety check needs. 여자 is a completely",
    "normal word and 여자를 타요 is not a sentence a learning product may generate;",
    "knowing that 여자 is a person and 타다 takes a vehicle is the only way to see it.",
    "",
    "Derived from the English meanings and then read by hand — the derivation put",
    "우유 among the animals, 마음 among the body parts and 별 among the people."
  ],
